# Discord Advanced Features

`Lux.Integrations.Discord.AdvancedFeatures` builds deterministic plans for voice channels, rich presence, webhooks, and server analytics.

The module does not open a Discord gateway session or stream audio directly. It returns payloads and policies that a Discord transport can execute with its own credentials and runtime supervision.

## Voice Channel Plan

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.Discord.AdvancedFeatures.voice_channel_plan(%{
  action: :join,
  guild_id: "111111111111111111",
  channel_id: "222222222222222222",
  queue: ["https://example.test/song.opus"]
})
```

## Rich Presence

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.Discord.AdvancedFeatures.rich_presence_plan(%{
  status: :online,
  activities: [%{type: :watching, name: "market alerts"}]
})
```

## Webhook Execution

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.Discord.AdvancedFeatures.webhook_plan(%{
  action: :execute,
  webhook_id: "333333333333333333",
  token: "token",
  content: "Trade filled",
  username: "Lux Bot"
})
```

## Server Analytics

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.Discord.AdvancedFeatures.analytics_report([
  %{type: :message, subtype: :command, user_id: "u1", channel_id: "commands"},
  %{type: :voice, user_id: "u1", channel_id: "voice", duration_seconds: 60}
])
```

The report includes activity by channel and hour, usage statistics, member counts, role frequencies, and a normalized event log.
